# Archive every cited source

When you add or update an **external citation URL** (page HTML, `sources.html`, or dossier JSON), snapshot it in the **same task**. Wayback Machine first. If Wayback cannot store a copy, try **archive.today**.

## Same-task steps

1. Save the live URL: `node scripts/archive_sources.js --url 'https://example.com/story'` (or `--save-missing` after a batch). Use `--archive-today-only --save-missing` when Wayback already failed and you only need the archive.today fallback.
2. Upsert `docs/source-archives.json`:
   - Prefer `wayback`, 14-digit `timestamp`, and ISO `captured`.
   - If Wayback has no snapshot, set `archive_today` (archive.today / archive.ph URL), `timestamp`, `captured`, and `method: "archive.today"`.
3. Keep the **live URL** as the primary `href`. Do not replace it with the archive.
4. Put a dated companion **beside** the live cite: `node scripts/inject_archive_companions.js` writes `<a class="source-archive"><time datetime="...">archived Mon. D, YYYY</time></a>` from the JSON. The companion `href` is Wayback when we have it, otherwise archive.today. `assets/source-archives.js` still fills any leftover at runtime. Do not hand-copy archive.org or archive.today URLs onto pages.
5. List `docs/source-archives.json` under On-site primary documents on `sources.html` (already there after the first import).

If Save Page Now fails, store the closest existing Wayback snapshot from the availability API or calendar redirect. If Wayback still has nothing, look up `https://archive.today/newest/{live URL}` and, if that 404s, submit the URL to archive.today. Never ship a new cite with no archive row (`wayback` or `archive_today`).

If archive.today returns **429** or a **CAPTCHA**, do not paste the article into `docs/`. Retry later, or ask the operator to submit the live URL in a browser. Leave the live cite in place until a snapshot URL exists.

## Skip

Same-site paths, `mailto:`, Maps / share-button endpoints, archive.org itself, and archive.today / archive.ph / archive.is mirrors.

```html
<!-- Live cite stays primary; inject_archive_companions.js adds the dated archive beside it -->
<a href="https://www.foxcarolina.com/story" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FOX Carolina</a>
<a class="source-archive" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20260814141415/https://www.foxcarolina.com/story" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Wayback Machine snapshot"><time datetime="2026-08-14T14:14:15Z">archived Aug. 14, 2026</time></a>
```
